14. Acceptance criteria per feature
6.1 Mailbox connection

OAuth flow completes and mailbox status shows "Connected" within 10s of consent grant
SMTP/IMAP test-connection fails gracefully with a specific error (auth failure vs network timeout vs wrong port) shown to the user, not a generic error
Revoked OAuth token is detected within 24h and mailbox status flips to "Reconnect required," surfaced in-app and via email notification
Credentials are never retrievable in plaintext via any API response or log

6.2 DNS wizard

All three record types (SPF/DKIM/DMARC) are independently verified with pass/fail state
Verify button reflects actual DNS state within propagation limits (retry guidance shown if just-published record isn't yet resolving)
Mailbox cannot enter warmup with zero verified records (at least SPF+DKIM required; DMARC can be "at risk" override)

6.3 Warmup engine

New mailbox starts at ≤5 emails/day and does not exceed defined ramp curve on any given day
Mailbox health score updates at least daily based on real inbox-placement data from the warmup pool
Auto-graduation only triggers when health score ≥ defined threshold AND minimum ramp duration met (both conditions required, not either/or)
Warmup sends never originate from a client's live campaign-sending domain

6.4 Campaign/sequence builder

A campaign cannot be launched if any attached mailbox is not "Warm" status (hard block, not warning)
Sequence respects per-mailbox and per-pool daily caps at send time, not just at scheduling time (i.e. caps are enforced even if manually edited mid-campaign)
AI-generated variants are distinguishably different per mailbox in the pool (no two mailboxes send byte-identical content in the same time window)
Conditional branches (opened/clicked/replied/no-reply) correctly evaluate before triggering the next step

6.5 List management

Duplicate leads (by email, case-insensitive) are never enrolled twice in the same campaign
Invalid/undeliverable emails (per verification check) are excluded from enrollment by default, with a visible count of excluded leads
Suppressed leads cannot be enrolled in any campaign, even via CSV re-import
List-Unsubscribe header is present on every send, and clicking it suppresses the lead within 1 minute

6.6 Unified inbox

Reply appears in unified inbox within 60 seconds of arriving (via push/webhook) or within the IMAP poll interval for SMTP mailboxes
Any reply auto-pauses that lead's sequence enrollment immediately, before the next scheduled step can fire
Classification accuracy is spot-checkable — misclassified replies can be manually recategorized and this doesn't break the paused state

6.7 Analytics

Bounce rate crossing threshold auto-pauses the mailbox within 1 hour of detection, not just flags it
Spam complaint rate is pulled from Postmaster Tools/SNDS on a defined schedule (e.g. daily) and reflected in the dashboard within 24h
All event counts (sent/opened/clicked/replied/bounced) reconcile — sent count per campaign equals sum of terminal states plus in-flight

6.8 Multi-tenancy

A workspace cannot see or query another workspace's mailboxes, leads, or campaigns under any account/permission combination
Shared infra (warmup pool, tracking domains) enforces per-tenant rate limits independent of other tenants' usage
15. Error & edge-case handling
Mailbox connection

OAuth consent denied by user → return to connection screen with clear retry option, no partial mailbox record created
Token revoked mid-campaign (client removes access from their Google/Microsoft account settings) → detect on next send attempt, pause affected campaigns for that mailbox only, notify client to reconnect
Same mailbox connected twice (by same or different workspace) → block duplicate connection within a workspace; flag but allow across workspaces (client may legitimately use one inbox for two purposes — log for abuse review)
SMTP server unreachable/times out repeatedly → after N consecutive failures, auto-pause mailbox and notify, don't keep retrying indefinitely

Sending

Mailbox hits provider's own daily limit (e.g. Gmail's ~500/day) mid-campaign → pause remaining sends for that mailbox until next day, redistribute to other pool mailboxes if pool has headroom
Send fails due to transient SMTP error (4xx) → retry with exponential backoff, cap retries, then mark as failed and alert
Send fails due to permanent error (5xx, invalid recipient) → treat as hard bounce, suppress immediately, don't retry

Warmup

Warmup pool partner mailbox itself is unhealthy/blacklisted → exclude it from the pool automatically rather than let it drag down partners' reputations
Client disconnects a mailbox mid-warmup → warmup schedule is cancelled, not paused/resumable indefinitely (re-connecting restarts warmup from scratch, since a gap invalidates ramp assumptions)

Replies/bounces

Auto-reply/OOO detected but misclassified as a real reply → sequence still pauses (safe default); client can manually resume
Bounce message format doesn't match known patterns (non-standard SMTP server) → falls back to a manual-review queue rather than silently ignoring it
Reply arrives after lead was already re-enrolled in a different campaign → most recent enrollment's sequence pauses; older/inactive enrollments unaffected

Limits/billing

Client hits plan limit (mailboxes, sends, or leads, depending on chosen model) mid-campaign → in-flight sends complete, new enrollments blocked, clear in-app upgrade prompt (never a silent hard stop mid-send)
Workspace deleted/downgraded while campaigns are active → campaigns pause, data retained for a defined grace period before purge, not deleted instantly

Compliance

Client attempts to launch a campaign without a verified unsubscribe mechanism → hard block at launch, not just a warning
Suppressed lead somehow re-enters via CSV or manual add → suppression check runs at enrollment time, not just at import time, so it's caught regardless of entry path

